Used by the vendor/Linux drivers as `FMC_OP_DMA`: rd_opcode/wr_opcode hold the SPI read/page-program opcode used by the DMA engine, rw_op selects the direction, and software sets dma_op_ready (bit 0) to start the DMA; the controller clears it when done. The reset value 0x00030200 is rd_opcode 0x03 (READ) and wr_opcode 0x02 (page program).

